The diagram shows a weighted network with $5$ vertices.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.2);
\coordinate (C) at (4,2);
\coordinate (D) at (3,0.3);
\coordinate (E) at (1,0.3);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above right] {$4$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, right] {$6$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below] {$3$};
\draw (E) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$7$};
\draw (B) -- (E) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the total weight of the minimum spanning tree?

